include ../../ui-overlay/ui-overlay.pug
include ../../../universal/button/button
+overlay()(id='js-endgame-overlay' class='EndgameOverlay')
  .conversationBox
    .conversation-container
      #part1
        p.SmallLabel SHIFT REVIEW / ORBIT WORKS
        h3 What caught your eye?
        p Which CV detail did you look at most?
        #buttons
          div.button.button__choice(role='button' tabindex='0' onclick='select(this)') Practical skill
          div.button.button__choice(role='button' tabindex='0' onclick='select(this)') Experience
          div.button.button__choice(role='button' tabindex='0' onclick='select(this)') School score
          div.button.button__choice(role='button' tabindex='0' onclick='select(this)') Ambition
      #part2
        h3 Your choices become examples.
        p Scout used past CVs and hiring choices. A hiring choice tells it what someone decided. It does not prove who could do the job.
        div.button.button__proceed(role='button' tabindex='0' onclick='next1()') Next →
      #part3
        h3 Look at the records too.
        p Adding more records does not automatically fix a problem. We need to ask who is in the records, who is missing, and what each label means.
        p What would you check before using another set of old hiring choices?
        div.button.button__proceed(role='button' tabindex='0' onclick='next2()') Next →
      #part4
        h3 A clue can hide in another detail.
        p Hiding city names may not remove every pattern. A school score can act as a clue to someone's city.
        p A quick answer is not enough. Check the data, the rules, and the results for both cities.
        .button-row
          a.button.button__proceed(href='../resources.html') How to play
          a.button.button__proceed(href='./') Play again
